# Local working memory: plans, progress logs, explanations.
# The skills in .claude/skills/ are committed; what they produce is not.
.claude/plans/

# The cursor is local. Nothing about the published calendar depends on it:
# links are recomputed from the channel on every run, so the scheduled job
# never reads or writes state. Only `pogocal poll` uses it, to report what is
# new on the machine it is run from — which is a per-machine question.
state/
